ItemTitle: Is the new ReasoningEffort parameter correctly mapped, validated, and applied across both the API request object and the chat model options?
Answer:
ChecklistItemAnswer[finalAnswer=The ReasoningEffort parameter is mapped to the API request object via @JsonProperty and included in the ChatCompletionRequest. It is also mapped to the chat model options via MistralAiChatOptions. However, the code does not demonstrate validation of the ReasoningEffort value (e.g., null handling, allowed values) beyond its presence in the builder and equals method., analysis=The provided code changes include explicit mapping of the ReasoningEffort parameter: it is added as a field in MistralAiChatOptions, validated via builder and equals method, and applied to the ChatCompletionRequest via @JsonProperty. The chat model also applies this metadata via buildMetadata. However, the evidence does not show validation of the ReasoningEffort value (e.g., null checks, allowed values) beyond its presence in the builder and equals method. The mapping is present but validation logic is minimal., evidence=[EvidenceItem[file=models/spring-ai-mistral-ai/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mistralai/MistralAiChatOptions.java, lines=105-112, reason=The code adds a private ReasoningEffort field and getter to MistralAiChatOptions, and includes ReasoningEffort in the builder and equals method, indicating mapping and validation.], EvidenceItem[file=models/spring-ai-mistral-ai/src/main/java/org/spring-ai-mistral-ai/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mistralai/MistralAiChatModel.java, lines=214-221, reason=The code includes a private Map<String, Object> buildMetadata method that uses constants REFERENCE_CONTENT_METADATA, REFERENCE_THINKING_CONTENT_METADATA, and THINKING_CONTENT_METADATA to store metadata from message content, showing application across chat model options.], EvidenceItem[file=models/spring-ai-mistral-ai/src/main/java/org/spring-ai-mistral-ai/src/main/java/org/springframework/ai/mistralai/api/MistralAiApi.java, lines=716-723, reason=The ChatCompletionRequest record now includes a @JsonProperty("reasoning_effort") field, mapping the ReasoningEffort parameter to the API request object.]]]
